    "['neighbor [parameter2] local-address [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': ['vpdn-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'vpdn-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200\\n neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- \"router bgp 100\" establishes the BGP process with AS 100 (implied from the Juniper group name AS100)\\n- \"neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200\" sets the peer AS number\\n- \"neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5\" is the Cisco equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"local-address\" parameter, specifying which local IP to use for the BGP session', 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200', 'parent_command': ['vpdn-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'vpdn-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200\\n neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- \"router bgp 100\" establishes the BGP process with AS 100 (implied from the Juniper group name AS100)\\n- \"neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200\" sets the peer AS number\\n- \"neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5\" is the Cisco equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"local-address\" parameter, specifying which local IP to use for the BGP session', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5', 'parent_command': ['vpdn-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'vpdn-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200\\n neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- \"router bgp 100\" establishes the BGP process with AS 100 (implied from the Juniper group name AS100)\\n- \"neighbor 10.0.7.7 remote-as 200\" sets the peer AS number\\n- \"neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5\" is the Cisco equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"local-address\" parameter, specifying which local IP to use for the BGP session', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.0.7.7 update-source 10.0.7.5'}]]": 1,
    "['neighbor [parameter2] local-address [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': ['vpdn-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'vpdn-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 1.1.1.1 update-source Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, we first enter BGP configuration mode with \"router bgp 100\" (using the same AS number)\\n- The \"neighbor 1.1.1.1 update-source Loopback0\" command sets the local address for BGP sessions with neighbor 1.1.1.1 to be sourced from the loopback interface (assuming Loopback0 is configured with address 1.1.1.2)\\n- Note that in Cisco, the loopback interface must be explicitly configured separately with the IP address 1.1.1.2', 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 1.1.1.1 update-source Loopback0', 'parent_command': ['vpdn-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'vpdn-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 1.1.1.1 update-source Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, we first enter BGP configuration mode with \"router bgp 100\" (using the same AS number)\\n- The \"neighbor 1.1.1.1 update-source Loopback0\" command sets the local address for BGP sessions with neighbor 1.1.1.1 to be sourced from the loopback interface (assuming Loopback0 is configured with address 1.1.1.2)\\n- Note that in Cisco, the loopback interface must be explicitly configured separately with the IP address 1.1.1.2', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 1.1.1.1 update-source Loopback0'}]]": 1,
